{% if shots -%}
This {{ duration }}-second clip is edited like a film scene: {{ shots | length }} shots with hard cuts between them,
at the times below. Every shot is filmed by a detached third-person observer camera.
{% set ns = namespace(t=0.0) -%}
{% for shot in shots -%}
[00:{{ "%04.1f" | format(ns.t) }}-00:{{ "%04.1f" | format(ns.t + shot.seconds) }}] {% if loop.first %}{{ shot.framing | capitalize }} shot exactly as the first frame{% else %}Hard cut to {{ "an" if shot.framing == "insert" else "a" }} {{ shot.framing }} shot{% endif %}: {{ shot.view }}
{% set ns.t = ns.t + shot.seconds -%}
{% endfor %}
What happens across the shots: {{ motion_prompt }}
Same people, same clothes, same place, same time of day and same light in every shot.
{% for o in outfits | default([]) -%}
In every shot, the person on the {{ o.position }} side of the first frame stays on that same side of the frame and keeps exactly this look: {{ o.look }}
{% endfor -%}
A reverse or reaction shot keeps everyone on the same side of the frame as in the first frame (do not cross the line).
In an over-the-shoulder shot, the blurred shoulder and back of the head in the foreground belong to the
OTHER person in the scene, recognizable by that person's own hair and clothes; the person facing the camera
never also appears in the foreground.
Everything a person holds or carries in the first frame (a bag, food, money, an umbrella) is still with the
same person in every later shot, with the same look, unless the action hands it over. Nothing vanishes between shots.
Every shot is the same room as the first frame: no new furniture, tables, chairs or rooms appear.
Every shot continues the same moment: people stand exactly where they stood and hands and objects stay
exactly where they were at the end of the previous shot. A reaction or over-the-shoulder shot starts no new action.
An insert shot is the same position seen closer: the hands stay at the same height in the air (or on the same
surface) as in the previous shot, with the same part of the room behind them; never move them onto a counter,
table or display case that is not right between the people in the first frame.
Nobody ever looks into the camera. No face fills the frame; an insert shot shows only hands or objects.
In every shot that is not an insert, each visible person's whole head and face stay inside the frame.
Each shot holds steady; any camera movement within a shot is very slow and minimal.
Make exactly these {{ shots | length }} shots and exactly {{ shots | length - 1 }} cuts. The last shot continues
unbroken to the very end of the clip; there is no cut after 00:{{ "%04.1f" | format(ns.t - shots[-1].seconds) }}.
{%- else -%}
{{ motion_prompt }}

The camera stays a detached third-person observer at a constant distance.
Any camera movement is very slow and minimal.
{%- endif %}
The colors, white balance, brightness and lighting stay exactly as in the first frame
for the whole clip. No color grading, tint or exposure change.
Every object stays solid and in place: anything a person holds stays in the same hand for the
whole shot, and nothing in the scene appears, disappears or changes shape.
Only the people and objects already in the first frame are in the shot; no one new enters.
{% if people | default([]) -%}
Exactly {{ people | length }} {{ "person is" if people | length == 1 else "different people are" }} in this clip and nobody else: {{ people | join("; ") }}.
Each of them appears only once in any frame: never two copies of the same person, no twins or look-alikes,
and no extra customers, passers-by or staff.
{% endif -%}
Each action happens once, in one direction, at a calm pace, and then the people hold still. Nothing is
repeated, undone or reversed: nothing is handed over and then taken back, or offered again and again.
{% if dialogue %}
There are exactly {{ dialogue | map(attribute='speaker') | unique | list | length }} different speaking voices in this scene. Each voice is distinct.
The shot opens with about one second of silence. Nobody speaks before the FIRST line below.
{% for line in dialogue %}
{% if line.position -%}
{% if loop.first %}FIRST{% else %}THEN{% endif %}, the person on the {{ line.position }} side of the frame{% if line.look %} ({{ line.look }}){% endif %} speaks{% if line.voice %}. Their voice is {{ line.voice }}{% endif %}.
Only that person's lips move, naturally in sync, as they say in Korean: "{{ line.text }}"
While they speak, everyone else stays silent with their mouth closed.
{% else -%}
{% if loop.first %}FIRST{% else %}THEN{% endif %}, an off-screen voice that is not anyone in the frame speaks (for example through a phone){% if line.voice %}. The voice is {{ line.voice }}{% endif %}.
It says in Korean: "{{ line.text }}"
Nobody in the frame moves their lips for this line; they only listen.
{% endif -%}
{% endfor %}
These are the ONLY words spoken in this shot. Nobody says anything else.
After the last line, everyone closes their mouth and stays completely silent
for the remainder of the shot. Do not invent additional dialogue or chatter
to fill the silence.
{{ mood_line }} No shouting.

{% if solo_side %}The speaker looks toward the other person just outside the frame on the {{ solo_side }} side, never at the camera.
Only this one person is in the frame.{% else %}The speakers look at each other while talking, never at the camera.{% endif %}

Absolutely no subtitles, captions, letters or any on-screen text appear at any time.
